Subject: [PATCH 03328/11362] [outer-loop] arc: TTT trust-gate LOO probe --
 prior+TTT path is DORMANT on unseen games (gate 0/5)

Gate-readiness measurement (operator-directed): does the prior-warmstarted gated-TTT path fire
on games the prior never saw? On all 5 LOO held-out games the trust gate (WorldModelVerifier
exact-grid-match >= 0.5) FIRES 0/5 for BOTH warm-start and scratch -- held-out exact-grid-match
accuracy = 0.0. Root cause: the gate metric is exact-FULL-GRID match, which a 64x64 CNN dynamics
model (0.55 changed-cell recall, ~0 exact-grid) can essentially never meet. So the prior's real
cell-recall gain (0.314->0.5485) is INVISIBLE to this gate, and the TTT path stays dormant on
unseen games -> contributes 0 to the hidden-game (0.08) score as currently wired. NOT gate-ready;
do not spend a scarce L4x4 shot on it. The exposed lever: a cell-recall/change-region trust metric
matched to the model's granularity (separate design+validation, not a this-week submission).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
